Print every environment variable the CLI reads, what it controls, whether it is set and the value in effect.
A variable that is not set shows the default in effect, which can come from the config file or the build.
Secrets are reported as set, never shown. Works offline and changes nothing.

Usage: agent-cli env

Flags:
  -h, --help     Print help
  -v, --verbose  Print diagnostic details to stderr

Examples:
  agent-cli env
  THE_AGENT_CLI_API_URL=https://agent.example.com agent-cli env

Environment: THE_AGENT_CLI_API_URL, THE_AGENT_CLI_HOME, THE_AGENT_CLI_TOKEN, THE_AGENT_CLI_PASSPHRASE, THE_AGENT_CLI_DEFAULT_CHAT, THE_AGENT_CLI_DEFAULT_PLATFORM, NO_COLOR
Exit codes: 0 ok · 1 failure (home directory or config file unusable) · 2 usage error
